# Byte-compiled / runtime
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so

# Packaging / build
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Testing / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# SIESTA / scratch outputs that may live next to the package
*.fdf
*.psml
*.xyz
*.pdb
*.ANI
*.XV
*.DM
*.bands
*.out
*.log

# But keep example fixtures if any are ever committed under tests/data/
!tests/data/**
# And keep frozen SIESTA .out fixtures for the parser dispatch tests.
# These are checked-in COPIES of historical runs, not active output.
!tests/watch/fixtures/**
# Same for tests/parse/: the .MD.nc reader is checked against the .out
# written by the SAME run, so the pair only proves anything together --
# committing one half would leave a test that cannot run.
!tests/parse/fixtures/**
# ...but a .parse.log is a BYPRODUCT the parser writes next to whatever it
# reads, not a fixture.  It regenerates on every run and would show up as a
# spurious diff.
tests/parse/fixtures/**/*.parse.log

# 3DNA archive / extracted tree if a user drops it next to the package
# during local install.  3DNA is distributed under a non-commercial-use
# license and must be downloaded directly from x3dna.org by the user
# (registration + license acceptance required).  These patterns are here
# both for dev hygiene and as a structural guard against accidentally
# committing the archive into the molbuilder repo, which would drag the
# molbuilder release under 3DNA's restricted terms.  See
# docs/design.md § "3DNA (canonical helix builder)".
x3dna-*.tar.gz
x3dna-*.zip
# Match the in-tree detector's permissive glob (see
# molbuilder/builders/backends/_threedna.py::_find_in_tree).
# Catches x3dna/, x3dna-v2.4/, x3dna-2.5/, x3dna-sep2025/ etc.
x3dna*/

.claude/
**/.claude/
claude-memory.tgz

# Per-machine config (TLS cert/key paths, OAuth client_id +
# client_secret_file paths, allowed_users allowlist, conda env
# name overrides).  NEVER commit the live file -- it likely
# points at credential files on disk (Let's Encrypt key, Google
# OAuth client_secret).  The committed template is
# ``docs/ops/examples/molbuilder.json.example`` (the ``.example``
# suffix keeps it from matching the pattern below).  Backups of the
# live config (molbuilder.json.bak*) must never be committed either.
molbuilder.json
molbuilder.json.bak*

# ...and the PROJECT-scope file, which is a different file with a
# similar name: `.molbuilder.json` (leading dot) sits in a project or
# calculation folder and carries that folder's `script_generation` /
# `scheduler` / `envs`.  It may not carry `auth`, `tls` or
# `secret_key_file` -- the runtime-config registry refuses those
# outside the machine scope -- so it is less sensitive than the file
# above, but it is still somebody's local setup and nothing in the
# repo is supposed to ship one.  The pattern above does NOT cover it:
# gitignore matches whole basenames, and `.molbuilder.json` is not
# `molbuilder.json`.  (The ones under `projects/` were already covered
# by `projects/*` below; this catches every other place a prepped
# folder can be unpacked.)
.molbuilder.json

# ...and EVERYTHING ELSE THAT LIVES BESIDE IT.  The block above ignores the
# config FILE; it was written before the config directory grew the rest of
# these, and a basename pattern only covers the name it spells.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS EVEN THOUGH THE CONFIG DIRECTORY IS NORMALLY OUTSIDE THE
# CHECKOUT: its location is an override.  `MOLBUILDER_CONFIG_DIR` names the
# root outright (configuration.md § 2.1c) and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` moves it too,
# so a person can legitimately point it at a path inside the repo -- and then
# `git add -A` would stage a session key, an OAuth client secret and a webhook
# URL.  Verified 2026-09-12: before these lines, `git check-ignore` said every
# one of them was trackable.
#
# Each has ONE fixed home in the config directory, so the basename is the
# right pattern; none of these names is tracked anywhere in the repo.
secret_key
google_client_secret
notify
notify_keys
secrets/
environments/
environment.json

projects/*
*.parse.log

# Persistent E2E failure diagnostics (capture_on_fail harness)
test-artifacts/

# live test-progress files (tools/testrun.py)
.test-progress/

# scratch for test runs and throwaway checks (never committed)
.testtmp/

# Third-party source that gets unpacked in the working tree -- never ours,
# and never small (2026-09-08: an 82 MB qe-7.5 pack reached origin via
# `git add -A`).  Both the archive AND what it unpacks to.
#
# ANCHORED AT THE ROOT ON PURPOSE.  Quantum ESPRESSO is an engine molbuilder
# is about to support, so `qe-*` unanchored -- which matches at EVERY depth --
# would silently swallow `molbuilder/qe-*.py`, `docs/engines/qe-*.md` and any
# test named for it.  The leading slash keeps it to the top level, where the
# tarball actually unpacks, and leaves the engine's own source free to be
# committed.
/qe-*
*.tar.gz
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.xz
*.tgz
